---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config/site.config';

const email = SITE.organization.email;
---

<PageLayout
  title="Contact"
  description={`Get in touch with the ${SITE.name} desk — story tips, corrections, AI tool submissions for the directory, and partnership or press enquiries.`}
  lede="Tips, corrections, tool submissions and press — here is how to reach the right desk."
>
  <p>
    Everything reaches one address:
    <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>. Use the subject-line prefixes below and your
    message gets routed to the right desk faster.
  </p>

  <!-- Owner: if you add a postal address later, put it here. [Your registered address] -->

  <h2>Story tips and pitches</h2>
  <p>
    Subject line <code>TIP</code>. Model releases, research you think is being under-covered,
    a lab or product story with something behind it, or a build you have shipped that would
    make a good tutorial. Include links to primary sources — a paper, a repo, a changelog, a
    model card. Tips backed by documents get read first.
  </p>
  <p>
    We do not pay for tips, and we will not name you unless you ask to be named.
  </p>

  <h2>Corrections</h2>
  <p>
    Subject line <code>CORRECTION</code>. Include the article URL and the exact claim you
    are disputing, plus a source we can check. Benchmark numbers, pricing tiers and context
    limits move quickly, so we would rather hear about a stale figure than leave it up.
  </p>
  <p>
    Corrections that change a conclusion or a recommendation are noted on the article with
    the date of the change. See the <a href="/editorial-policy/">editorial policy</a> for
    how we handle them.
  </p>

  <h2>Tool and agent submissions</h2>
  <p>
    Subject line <code>DIRECTORY</code>. To be considered for the
    <a href="/tools/">AI tool directory</a> or the
    <a href="/agents/">AI agent directory</a>, send:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Product name, homepage URL and a one-sentence description of what it does.</li>
    <li>The category it belongs in and what it competes with.</li>
    <li>Pricing structure — free tier, individual plan, team, enterprise.</li>
    <li>Docs or API reference, and a way for us to try it without a sales call.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Listings are free and cannot be bought. We do not accept payment for inclusion,
    position or rating, and a submission is not a guarantee of a listing. Prompt
    contributions for the <a href="/prompts/">prompt library</a> use the same address.
  </p>

  <h2>Partnerships and press</h2>
  <p>
    Subject line <code>PARTNER</code> for sponsorship, syndication, licensing or content
    partnerships, and <code>PRESS</code> for interview requests, commentary or analyst
    briefings. Include your deadline. Sponsorship never buys editorial coverage or a
    directory position — the two are handled separately and disclosed where relevant.
  </p>

  <h2>Website and security issues</h2>
  <p>
    Subject line <code>SECURITY</code> for a vulnerability in this site, or
    <code>BUG</code> for anything broken — a dead link, a rendering problem, a bad search
    result. Include the URL and your browser. We do not run a paid bounty, and we will
    credit reporters who want credit.
  </p>

  <h2>What we do not accept</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Paid guest posts, sponsored articles or link insertions.</li>
    <li>Requests to remove or soften accurate published reporting.</li>
    <li>Unsolicited fully AI-generated article submissions.</li>
    <li>Payment in exchange for a directory listing, a rating or a review outcome.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    The reasoning is in the <a href="/editorial-policy/">editorial policy</a> and the
    <a href="/disclaimer/">disclaimer</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Data and privacy requests</h2>
  <p>
    Subject line <code>PRIVACY</code> for access, correction or deletion requests. What we
    hold and how long we hold it is described in the
    <a href="/privacy-policy/">privacy policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Response times</h2>
  <p>
    This is a small desk. Security reports and corrections are triaged within two business
    days; everything else may take longer. We read everything and reply to anything that
    needs a reply.
  </p>
</PageLayout>
